lt rifle as he  applauded his security forces  they forced opposition leader svetlana  tikanovskaya  into exile in neighboring lithuania  i believe in our people and i'm sure  that  we will not lose this moment what's  going to happen to you  remains in belarus our voice cannot be  ignored she told me  everything will be fine with me shortly  thereafter  she was detained and sentenced to 10  days in prison for unauthorized protests  long-lived belarus they shout a call to  action  despite ongoing threats from the  president says andre dimitriev  an opposition candidate if you could say  one thing to president lukashenko right  now what would it be  please leave us a somber scene at the  funeral and a grim one here in these  woods where that young protester's body  was  found the protesters say that was an act  to intimidate them but that in the end  only made them stronger for cbs this  morning saturday chris livesay minsk  belarus
 

